					],
					"source": "\\begin{dmath*}{}0\\,\\end{dmath*}"
				}
			],
			"source": "chk2:= @(dL2) - @(eins);\ncanonicalise(chk2)\nrename_dummies(chk2)\ncollect_terms(chk2);"
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 4436317864282661553,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "latex",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 4436317864282661553,
					"cell_origin": "client",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"source": "Only the antisymmetry of $R_{\\mu\\nu}{}^{mn}$ in both index pairs was used here. The pair\nexchange symmetry does not hold, because the connection $\\omega(e,\\psi)$ has torsion."
				}
			],
			"hidden": true,
			"source": "Only the antisymmetry of $R_{\\mu\\nu}{}^{mn}$ in both index pairs was used here. The pair\nexchange symmetry does not hold, because the connection $\\omega(e,\\psi)$ has torsion."
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 4763711306635414724,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "latex",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 4763711306635414724,
					"cell_origin": "client",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"source": "\\subsection*{Variation of the gravitini}\n\nThe gravitino appears twice in $\\mathcal{L}^{(3/2)}$, so varying it gives two terms:\none with $\\delta\\psi_\\rho = D_\\rho\\epsilon$ and one with\n$\\delta\\bar\\psi_\\mu = \\overline{D_\\mu\\epsilon}$."
				}
			],
			"hidden": true,
			"source": "\\subsection*{Variation of the gravitini}\n\nThe gravitino appears twice in $\\mathcal{L}^{(3/2)}$, so varying it gives two terms:\none with $\\delta\\psi_\\rho = D_\\rho\\epsilon$ and one with\n$\\delta\\bar\\psi_\\mu = \\overline{D_\\mu\\epsilon}$."
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 7100106131957779036,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "input",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 6283153382889052647,
					"cell_origin": "server",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"cells": [
						{
							"cell_id": 6275617277741929721,
							"cell_origin": "server",
							"cell_type": "input_form",
							"source": "\\psi_{\\mu} -> D_{\\mu}(\\epsilon)"
						}
					],
					"source": "\\begin{dmath*}{}\\psi_{\\mu} \\rightarrow D_{\\mu}{\\epsilon}\\end{dmath*}"
				},
				{
					"cell_id": 7872901004653232381,
					"cell_origin": "server",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"cells": [
						{
							"cell_id": 10668205259124335037,
							"cell_origin": "server",
							"cell_type": "input_form",
							"source": " -  1/2 e \\bar{\\psi_{\\mu}} \\Gamma^{m n p} D_{\\nu}(\\psi_{\\rho}) e_{m}^{\\mu} e_{n}^{\\nu} e_{p}^{\\rho}"
						}
					],
					"source": "\\begin{dmath*}{} - \\frac{1}{2}\\,e \\bar{\\psi_{\\mu}} \\Gamma^{m n p} D_{\\nu}{\\psi_{\\rho}} e_{m}\\,^{\\mu} e_{n}\\,^{\\nu} e_{p}\\,^{\\rho}\\end{dmath*}"
				},
				{
					"cell_id": 14893154796701981938,
					"cell_origin": "server",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"cells": [
						{
							"cell_id": 10062172591858604424,
							"cell_origin": "server",
							"cell_type": "input_form",
							"source": " -  1/2 e \\bar{D_{\\mu}(\\epsilon)} \\Gamma^{m n p} D_{\\nu}(\\psi_{\\rho}) e_{m}^{\\mu} e_{n}^{\\nu} e_{p}^{\\rho} -  1/2 e \\bar{\\psi_{\\mu}} \\Gamma^{m n p} D_{\\nu}(D_{\\rho}(\\epsilon)) e_{m}^{\\mu} e_{n}^{\\nu} e_{p}^{\\rho}"
						}
					],
					"source": "\\begin{dmath*}{} - \\frac{1}{2}\\,e \\bar{D_{\\mu}{\\epsilon}} \\Gamma^{m n p} D_{\\nu}{\\psi_{\\rho}} e_{m}\\,^{\\mu} e_{n}\\,^{\\nu} e_{p}\\,^{\\rho}\\discretionary{}{}{} - \\frac{1}{2}\\,e \\bar{\\psi_{\\mu}} \\Gamma^{m n p} D_{\\nu}{D_{\\rho}{\\epsilon}} e_{m}\\,^{\\mu} e_{n}\\,^{\\nu} e_{p}\\,^{\\rho}\\end{dmath*}"
				}
			],
			"source": "dpsi:= { \\psi_{\\mu} -> D_{\\mu}{\\epsilon} };\ndL32:= @(L32);\nvary(dL32, dpsi);"
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 1999065386350794571,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "latex",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 1999065386350794571,
					"cell_origin": "client",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"source": "In the first term the two derivatives in $D_\\nu D_\\rho\\epsilon$ are antisymmetrised by\n$\\Gamma^{mnp}e_n{}^\\nu e_p{}^\\rho$, so we can replace them by half the commutator.\n$D_\\mu$ contains no Christoffel connection, so no torsion term appears, and the curvature\ncheck at the top gives $D_\\nu D_\\rho\\epsilon \\to \\tfrac18 R_{\\nu\\rho}{}^{mn}\\Gamma_{mn}\\epsilon$\n(vN~1.7 eq.~(3))."
				}
			],
			"hidden": true,
			"source": "In the first term the two derivatives in $D_\\nu D_\\rho\\epsilon$ are antisymmetrised by\n$\\Gamma^{mnp}e_n{}^\\nu e_p{}^\\rho$, so we can replace them by half the commutator.\n$D_\\mu$ contains no Christoffel connection, so no torsion term appears, and the curvature\ncheck at the top gives $D_\\nu D_\\rho\\epsilon \\to \\tfrac18 R_{\\nu\\rho}{}^{mn}\\Gamma_{mn}\\epsilon$\n(vN~1.7 eq.~(3))."
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 8723932739694799219,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "input",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 11885174235014343986,
					"cell_origin": "server",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"cells": [
						{
							"cell_id": 9838169647651943456,
							"cell_origin": "server",
							"cell_type": "input_form",
							"source": " -  1/2 e \\bar{D_{\\mu}(\\epsilon)} \\Gamma^{m n p} D_{\\nu}(\\psi_{\\rho}) e_{m}^{\\mu} e_{n}^{\\nu} e_{p}^{\\rho} -  1/2 e \\bar{\\psi_{\\mu}} \\Gamma^{m n p} D_{\\nu}(D_{\\rho}(\\epsilon)) e_{m}^{\\mu} e_{n}^{\\nu} e_{p}^{\\rho}"
						}
					],
					"source": "\\begin{dmath*}{} - \\frac{1}{2}\\,e \\bar{D_{\\mu}{\\epsilon}} \\Gamma^{m n p} D_{\\nu}{\\psi_{\\rho}} e_{m}\\,^{\\mu} e_{n}\\,^{\\nu} e_{p}\\,^{\\rho}\\discretionary{}{}{} - \\frac{1}{2}\\,e \\bar{\\psi_{\\mu}} \\Gamma^{m n p} D_{\\nu}{D_{\\rho}{\\epsilon}} e_{m}\\,^{\\mu} e_{n}\\,^{\\nu} e_{p}\\,^{\\rho}\\end{dmath*}"
				},
