						}
					],
					"source": "\\begin{dmath*}{} - \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\int \\left(-\\,D_{\\mu}{e} \\bar{\\epsilon} \\Gamma^{m n p} D_{\\nu}{\\psi_{\\rho}} e_{m}\\,^{\\mu} e_{n}\\,^{\\nu} e_{p}\\,^{\\rho}\\discretionary{}{}{}-\\,e \\bar{\\epsilon} D_{\\mu}\\left(\\Gamma^{m n p} D_{\\nu}{\\psi_{\\rho}} e_{m}\\,^{\\mu} e_{n}\\,^{\\nu} e_{p}\\,^{\\rho}\\right)\\right)\\,\\,{\\rm d}x\\end{dmath*}"
				}
			],
			"source": "ib:= \\int{ @(dpsibar) }{x};\nintegrate_by_parts(ib, $\\bar{\\epsilon}$);"
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 3338630900317530677,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "latex",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 3338630900317530677,
					"cell_origin": "client",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"source": "After this the integral sign has done its job, and we remove it again. The derivative $D_\\mu$\nnow acts on the determinant, the inverse vielbeine, the gamma matrix and $D_\\nu\\psi_\\rho$.\nA gamma matrix with flat indices is covariantly constant. The derivatives of the determinant and of\nthe inverse vielbeine can all be written in terms of $D_\\mu e^q{}_\\lambda$. This is not zero,\nbecause $D_\\mu$ contains only the spin connection (see vN~1.4 below eq.~(3)):\n\\begin{equation*}\nD_\\mu e = e\\, e_q{}^\\lambda D_\\mu e^q{}_\\lambda\\,,\\qquad\nD_\\mu e_m{}^\\nu = - e_m{}^\\lambda (D_\\mu e^q{}_\\lambda)\\, e_q{}^\\nu\\,.\n\\end{equation*}"
				}
			],
			"hidden": true,
			"source": "After this the integral sign has done its job, and we remove it again. The derivative $D_\\mu$\nnow acts on the determinant, the inverse vielbeine, the gamma matrix and $D_\\nu\\psi_\\rho$.\nA gamma matrix with flat indices is covariantly constant. The derivatives of the determinant and of\nthe inverse vielbeine can all be written in terms of $D_\\mu e^q{}_\\lambda$. This is not zero,\nbecause $D_\\mu$ contains only the spin connection (see vN~1.4 below eq.~(3)):\n\\begin{equation*}\nD_\\mu e = e\\, e_q{}^\\lambda D_\\mu e^q{}_\\lambda\\,,\\qquad\nD_\\mu e_m{}^\\nu = - e_m{}^\\lambda (D_\\mu e^q{}_\\lambda)\\, e_q{}^\\nu\\,.\n\\end{equation*}"
		},
