			"source": "tot:= @(curv) + @(dL2);\nsort_product(tot)\ncanonicalise(tot)\nrename_dummies(tot)\ncollect_terms(tot);"
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 5177686213858675915,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "latex",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 5177686213858675915,
					"cell_origin": "client",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"source": "This also confirms that $\\mathcal{L}^{(3/2)}$ has the right normalisation and sign relative\nto the Hilbert action, so the $\\Gamma^{\\mu\\nu\\rho}$ form is equivalent to vN's\n$\\epsilon^{\\mu\\nu\\rho\\sigma}\\gamma_5\\gamma_\\nu$ form.\n\nWhat is left is the expression \\verb|dDe| with derivatives of the vielbein, and the\nvariation of the explicit vielbeine in $\\mathcal{L}^{(3/2)}$ (vN~1.7 eq.~(10)).\nTo show that these cancel we need the torsion equation for $D_{[\\mu}e^a{}_{\\nu]}$ and a Fierz\nrearrangement; that comes next."
				}
			],
			"hidden": true,
			"source": "This also confirms that $\\mathcal{L}^{(3/2)}$ has the right normalisation and sign relative\nto the Hilbert action, so the $\\Gamma^{\\mu\\nu\\rho}$ form is equivalent to vN's\n$\\epsilon^{\\mu\\nu\\rho\\sigma}\\gamma_5\\gamma_\\nu$ form.\n\nWhat is left is the expression \\verb|dDe| with derivatives of the vielbein, and the\nvariation of the explicit vielbeine in $\\mathcal{L}^{(3/2)}$ (vN~1.7 eq.~(10)).\nTo show that these cancel we need the torsion equation for $D_{[\\mu}e^a{}_{\\nu]}$ and a Fierz\nrearrangement; that comes next."
		},
